<article class="page">
  <header>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">This site does not track you. No cookies, no analytics, no fonts or scripts
       loaded from other companies. What follows is the little that remains, which any
       website involves.</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="who">
    <h2 id="who">Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>The data controller is Salvatore Di Dio, who runs this site in a personal capacity.
       Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> for anything concerning
       your data. No data protection officer has been appointed: the law does not require one
       for a site like this.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="not">
    <h2 id="not">What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device: no local storage, no
          identifiers. That is why there is no cookie banner.</li>
      <li>It has no analytics. I do not know who visits, or how many.</li>
      <li>It contacts no other company while a page loads. Fonts are the ones already on
          your device; images and styles come from this site.</li>
      <li>It has no forms, no accounts and no newsletter.</li>
      <li>It makes no automated decisions and builds no profiles.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="hosting">
    <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, run by GitHub, and delivered through Fastly. When
       you open a page, GitHub
       <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages">logs
       your IP address for security purposes</a>, as any web server must receive it to send
       you the page. That logging happens under
       <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's
       privacy statement</a>, which also covers transfers outside the European Union: GitHub
       is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and relies on the European
       Commission's standard contractual clauses. I have no access to these logs.</p>
    <p>The legal basis is legitimate interest (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR): publishing the site and
       keeping it secure.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="email">
    <h2 id="email">If you write to me</h2>
    <p>Email sent to {{ site.email }} reaches me through the University of Palermo's email
       service. I use your address and what you write only to reply and to follow up on what
       you asked. I do not share it, and I do not add you to any list.</p>
    <p>The legal basis is my legitimate interest in answering the people who write to me
       (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Writing is voluntary; without an address I cannot reply.
       I keep the exchange for as long as the conversation needs it, and no longer than
       24 months after the last message, unless it turns into a collaboration that requires
       keeping it.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="video">
    <h2 id="video">Videos</h2>
    <p>Talks are shown as a plain link. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you click. When
       you do, the player loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, run by Google: from that
       moment Google receives your IP address and may store data on your device, under
       <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>. If you would
       rather not, follow the link and watch the video on YouTube directly, or don't.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="links">
    <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Links lead to other websites, such as the University of Palermo, MUV, PUSH, ORCID and
       LinkedIn, and open in a new tab. Once you follow one, that site's own privacy policy applies.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="rights">
    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to access the data I hold about you, to correct it, to delete it, to limit
       its use, or to receive it in a portable format (Articles 15–20 GDPR). Because I rely on
       legitimate interest, you also have the right to object at any time (Article 21).
       Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
    <p>You can lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection authority, the
       <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/">Garante per la protezione dei dati
       personali</a>, or with the authority of the country where you live or work.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="changes">
    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>If anything above changes, such as a new service, a form or anything that touches your
       data, this page changes first. Last updated {{ updated | readableDate }}.</p>
  </section>
</article>
